---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="A production-ready MCP server for Jira Cloud and Data Center." />
    <title>Jira MCP | Jira for your AI tools</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="shell">
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Jira MCP home">
          <span class="brand-mark">J</span>
          <span>jira-mcp</span>
        </a>
        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/lucaswilliameufrasio/jira-mcp">GitHub</a>
          <a href="#quick-start">Quick start</a>
          <a class="nav-cta" href="https://github.com/lucaswilliameufrasio/jira-mcp/releases">Releases</a>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> Open-source MCP server</p>
          <h1>Give your AI a direct line to Jira.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Search, create, update and move issues from any MCP host. Local stdio for a single developer, remote OAuth for teams.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="#quick-start">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/lucaswilliameufrasio/jira-mcp">View source</a>
          </div>
          <div class="trust-row"><span>Cloud v3</span><span>Data Center v2</span><span>OAuth + PKCE</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example setup command">
          <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><small>terminal</small></div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <p><b class="green">$</b> jira-mcp setup</p>
            <p class="muted">Jira URL: https://acme.atlassian.net</p>
            <p class="muted">Deployment (cloud/server): cloud</p>
            <p class="muted">Jira email: you@acme.com</p>
            <p class="muted">Jira API token: ********</p>
            <p><b class="green">&#10003;</b> Ready. Connect your MCP host.</p>
            <p class="cursor">&#9608;</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-grid" aria-label="Features">
        <article><span class="icon">01</span><h2>Native MCP</h2><p>Official Go SDK and protocol-level tests. Works with OpenCode and any compatible host.</p></article>
        <article><span class="icon">02</span><h2>Two deployment modes</h2><p>Stdio for local use. Streamable HTTP with Atlassian OAuth for shared infrastructure.</p></article>
        <article><span class="icon">03</span><h2>Built to be trusted</h2><p>PKCE, encrypted tokens, isolated users, Valkey sessions and contract-tested Jira APIs.</p></article>
      </section>

      <section class="quick-start" id="quick-start">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Local setup</p><h2>Connect in under a minute.</h2><p>Download a release or build from source, then let the setup wizard create a local configuration with restrictive permissions.</p></div>
        <pre><code><span class="comment"># build</span>
go build -o jira-mcp .

<span class="comment"># configure</span>
./jira-mcp setup

<span class="comment"># run over stdio</span>
./jira-mcp</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="footer-cta">
        <p class="eyebrow">Made for the MCP ecosystem</p>
        <h2>Less tab switching. More shipping.</h2>
        <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/lucaswilliameufrasio/jira-mcp">Explore Jira MCP <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
      </section>

      <footer><span>&copy; 2026 Jira MCP</span><span>Open source under the project license</span></footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) { margin: 0; background: #101311; color: #eff3e9; font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; }
  :global(a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .shell { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 28px; overflow: hidden; }
  .nav { height: 84px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px solid #293128; }
  .brand, .nav-links, .hero-actions, .trust-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; }
  .brand { gap: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
  .brand-mark { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 8px; background: #d8fa5c; color: #11150f; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 20px; }
  .nav-links { color: #a9b1a2; font-size: 14px; }
  .nav-links a:hover { color: #d8fa5c; }
  .nav-cta { border: 1px solid #475441; border-radius: 999px; padding: 9px 15px; color: #eff3e9; }
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr .95fr; gap: 90px; align-items: center; min-height: 590px; padding: 76px 0 92px; }
  .eyebrow { color: #d8fa5c; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .pulse { display: inline-block; width: 7px; height: 7px; margin-right: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: #d8fa5c; box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px #d8fa5c1c; vertical-align: 1px; }
  h1, h2 { letter-spacing: -.055em; line-height: .98; margin: 0; }
  h1 { max-width: 700px; font-size: clamp(54px, 7vw, 88px); font-weight: 650; }
  h2 { font-size: 30px; }
  .lede { max-width: 530px; margin: 28px 0 32px; color: #a9b1a2; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; border-radius: 999px; padding: 13px 18px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; }
  .primary { background: #d8fa5c; color: #11150f; }
  .secondary { border: 1px solid #475441; color: #eff3e9; }
  .trust-row { margin-top: 52px; color: #778174; font-size: 12px; }
  .trust-row span + span { border-left: 1px solid #3a4339; padding-left: 22px; }
  .terminal { background: #171c18; border: 1px solid #354033; border-radius: 14px; box-shadow: 22px 24px 0 #0b0e0c; transform: rotate(1.5deg); }
  .terminal-bar { display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #2d362d; }
  .terminal-bar span { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: #4c564c; }
  .terminal-bar small { margin-left: auto; color: #697367; font: 11px ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .terminal-body { padding: 25px 22px; color: #dfe9d8; font: 13px/2 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace; }
  .terminal-body p { margin: 0; }.green { color: #d8fa5c; }.muted { color: #7f8b7d; }.cursor { color: #d8fa5c; }
  .feature-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: #354033; border: 1px solid #354033; }
  .feature-grid article { min-height: 230px; padding: 29px; background: #151a16; }.icon { color: #d8fa5c; font: 12px ui-monospace, monospace; }.feature-grid h2 { margin: 22px 0 12px; font-size: 22px; }.feature-grid p, .quick-start p { color: #929d90; line-height: 1.6; }
  .quick-start { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: 90px; align-items: center; padding: 145px 50px; }.quick-start h2 { font-size: 46px; }.quick-start pre { margin: 0; padding: 25px; overflow: auto; border: 1px solid #354033; border-radius: 12px; background: #151a16; color: #dfe9d8; line-height: 1.8; }.comment { color: #6f806a; }
  .footer-cta { padding: 90px 0 110px; text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid #293128; }.footer-cta h2 { margin: 20px auto 30px; font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 70px); }.footer-cta .button { margin-top: 5px; }
  footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 20px 0 28px; color: #697367; font-size: 12px; border-top: 1px solid #293128; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .shell { padding: 0 18px; }.nav-links a:not(.nav-cta) { display: none; }.hero { display: block; padding: 65px 0 75px; }.hero-copy { margin-bottom: 65px; } .hero h1 { font-size: 57px; }.feature-grid, .quick-start { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.quick-start { gap: 35px; padding: 90px 0; }.quick-start h2 { font-size: 39px; }.terminal { transform: none; box-shadow: 10px 12px 0 #0b0e0c; } footer { gap: 20px; flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
